.TH MU2EDAQ\-DISCOVERY 7 "2026-09-30" "mu2edaq-discovery 1.1.0" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2edaq\-discovery \- UDP service discovery protocol for the Mu2e DAQ suite
.SH SYNOPSIS
.EX
Protocol identifier   mu2edaq-discovery/1
Multicast group       239.255.42.99
Broadcast             255.255.255.255 (or a subnet broadcast address)
UDP port              28999
Encoding              one UTF-8 JSON object per datagram
Maximum datagram      1400 bytes
Message types         DISCOVER (query), ANNOUNCE (response/unsolicited)
.EE
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B mu2edaq\-discovery
is the substrate the whole Mu2e DAQ Python suite uses to answer "what is
running, on which node, on which port".
A service embeds a responder and becomes findable; an operator runs
.BR mu2edaq\-discover (1)
or
.BR mu2edaq\-discover\-gui (1)
and sees it.
.PP
The design is deliberately minimal: no registry, no broker, no persistent
state, no authentication.
Every responder is authoritative only for itself, and a scan is a snapshot of
who answered within the timeout.
Nothing is remembered between scans, so a service that dies simply stops
appearing.
.SH PROTOCOL
.SS DISCOVER
Sent by a client, to the multicast group and to the broadcast address
together, or unicast to one host.
.EX
    {"proto": "mu2edaq-discovery/1",
     "type":  "DISCOVER",
     "qid":   "9f1c2e34-5d6a-4b7c-8e9f-0a1b2c3d4e5f",
     "filter": {"app": "vnc"}}
.EE
.TP
.B qid
Required string, a UUID4 generated per query.
Responders echo it so a client can discard replies to an earlier query.
.TP
.B filter
Optional object.
Keys may be
.BR app ", " name " or " host
only; values are
.BR fnmatch (3)\-style
globs matched against the corresponding ANNOUNCE fields.
All named keys must match.
A responder that does not match must not reply.
An absent or empty filter matches everything.
.SS ANNOUNCE
Sent unicast back to the DISCOVER's source address and port, after a uniform
random delay of 0 to 250 ms that prevents a reply storm when a whole cluster
answers at once.
.EX
    {"proto":   "mu2edaq-discovery/1",
     "type":    "ANNOUNCE",
     "qid":     "9f1c2e34-5d6a-4b7c-8e9f-0a1b2c3d4e5f",
     "id":      "c0ffee12-3456-4789-abcd-ef0123456789",
     "name":    "VNC mu2e-dl-01 :1 (daq-main)",
     "app":     "vnc",
     "host":    "mu2e-dl-01.fnal.gov",
     "port":    5901,
     "scheme":  "vnc",
     "version": "1.0",
     "pid":     12345,
     "started": "2026-06-12T15:04:05Z",
     "meta":    {"display": ":1", "geometry": "2560x1440"}}
.EE
.TP
.B id
Required string, a UUID4 generated once per responder object.
It is the deduplication key: a client that receives the same
.B id
by multicast, by broadcast and on a retransmission counts one service.
.TP
.B port ", " pid
Required JSON integers.
A string here is a protocol error; booleans are rejected too.
.TP
.B meta
Optional object whose keys and values must all be strings.
Consumers render it as
.BI meta. key
columns, so a responder can publish new detail without any client change.
.TP
.B qid
Present on a solicited reply, absent on an unsolicited periodic announcement.
.PP
A responder configured with a non\-zero announce interval also multicasts the
same ANNOUNCE, without
.BR qid ,
to the group at that interval, for passive listeners.
.SS Transport
A DISCOVER may arrive three ways and a responder treats them alike, always
replying unicast to the datagram's source.
.TP
.B Multicast
.BR 239.255.42.99:28999 .
Reaches hosts that joined the group, as far as IGMP snooping and multicast
routing allow.
.TP
.B Broadcast
.BR 255.255.255.255:28999 ,
or a subnet's own broadcast address.
Reaches every host on the sender's subnet, and is not subject to IGMP
snooping.
.TP
.B Unicast
.IB host :28999 .
Reaches that host.
.PP
Since version 1.1.0 clients send the multicast and the broadcast together and
merge the replies by
.BR id .
The broadcast leg was added because the Mu2e DAQ switches run IGMP snooping
with no querier: each switch forwards the group only to ports it has seen
join, membership never propagates between switches, and a multicast scan
therefore sees only the scanner's own switch.
Responders needed no change, since they bind
.BR 0.0.0.0 .
The network\-side remedy is an IGMP querier on the VLAN.
.PP
Neither multicast nor broadcast crosses a router or the FNAL gateway.
From off site, run the scan on a cluster node over ssh.
.SS Size limit
A datagram must not exceed 1400 bytes, chosen to fit one Ethernet MTU with
headers and so never fragment.
The limit is on the serialized message, so a large
.B meta
map or a long
.B name
can cross it at runtime.
Both encode and decode enforce it in the Python implementation; the C++
responder does not check the ANNOUNCE it builds.
.SS Address family
IPv4 only, throughout.
The sockets are
.BR AF_INET ,
the group membership uses
.BR ip_mreq ,
and there is no IPv6 group or dual\-stack path in either implementation.
.SH IMPLEMENTATIONS
.TP
.B Python
.BR mu2edaq_discovery (3).
Client and responder, stdlib only, Python 3.9.
Embedded by the Python services in the suite.
.TP
.B C++
.BR libmu2edaq_discovery (3).
Responder only, C++17 and POSIX sockets, consumed by CMake
.BR FetchContent .
.TP
.B Embedded fallback
.B mu2edaq\-controlroom\-setup
ships
.I server/vnc-discovery-responder.py
with a hand\-copied responder used when the package is not importable, so a
VNC session is discoverable on a host with no virtualenv.
It is a fourth copy of the wire format and must be kept in step by hand.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I doc/PROTOCOL.md
The protocol specification this page summarises.
.TP
.I config/discovery.yaml
Example configuration; see
.BR discovery.yaml (5).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_GROUP
.TQ
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_PORT
.TQ
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_TIMEOUT
.TQ
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_INTERVAL
.TQ
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_BROADCAST
.TQ
.B MU2EDAQ_DISCOVERY_CONFIG
Read by the front\-end commands, not by the library.
.SH EXAMPLES
See what answers on the local subnet:
.EX
    mu2edaq-discover
.EE
Probe one node directly, bypassing both multicast and broadcast, to prove the
responder is alive:
.EX
    printf '{"proto":"mu2edaq-discovery/1","type":"DISCOVER","qid":"x"}' \\
        | nc -u -w2 mu2e-dl-01.fnal.gov 28999
.EE
.SH SECURITY CONSIDERATIONS
There is no authentication and no integrity protection.
Any host on the subnet can send a DISCOVER and learn the full inventory of
services, their ports, their process IDs and their uptimes, and any host can
send a forged ANNOUNCE that a scan will display as real.
The protocol is intended for the private DAQ VLAN only and must not be exposed
to a routed or untrusted network.
.SH NOTES
Port 28999 was chosen to avoid every port already in use in the suite: 9999
.RB ( heartbeatmonitor ),
37020
.RB ( bigredbox ),
5555 and 5556 (dashboard ZMQ and trigger scalers), 9876
.RB ( controlcenter ),
7755
.RB ( dataformat\-viewer ),
and the 5000 to 8088 HTTP range.
.PP
The package is not published on PyPI.
Naming
.B mu2edaq\-discovery
in a
.I requirements.txt
aborts the whole pip resolve; use
.I mu2edaq-install-discovery.sh
at the superproject root instead.
